      "writtenOn": "2021-06-02T01:35:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this seems more complicated than it needs to be. The put and alloc are always newer than get. The old code should have produced the correct result in with ubsan disabled as put - get is the same as 0x100000000 + put - get for a uint32_t value.\n\nIf the log buffer size is not a power of two, wrapping when a uint32 wraps will loose information anyway.\n\nWe can fix the overflow cases by using ubsan safe functions like check_add_overflow for the current power-of-2 only buffer sizes",
      "revId": "135b8a02b28000bab3dfc01947a4a3466d15bb47",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
